{%- comment -%}
  Wig Party — mega menu panel for ONE parent nav item.

  ARCHITECTURE. There is one dedicated block type per parent menu —
  `shop_mega_menu`, `best_sellers_mega_menu`, `start_here_mega_menu`, `live_mega_menu`,
  `community_mega_menu`, `daily_deals_mega_menu` — and this snippet holds each one's PRESET
  layout. Everything the Figma frames already decide lives here as literal arguments:
  the Shopify menu handles, the column order and types, the column widths and card
  heights, the icons, the column gap and which column starts the right-hand group.

  That means the Theme Editor exposes only what a merchant can sensibly change (images,
  copy, CTA links, a product source). No handles to paste, no parent labels to type, no
  child-menu wiring, no column-type pickers.

  Adding a seventh parent menu is: one block type in the schema, one `when` branch here.

  APPROVED FRAMES — client file GwwzFncuGYte0VMIN8G9UV, page 6337:3110
  ("Navigation - For Developer"). These SUPERSEDE the earlier V4 6316:* frames; the two
  sets differ (no shell behind the Best Sellers row, no photo on the Community card, a
  visible chevron on the open parent, sharper Deals corners), so do not mix them.
    Shop 6337:4768 · Best Sellers 6337:3148 · Start Here 6337:3448
    Live 6337:3786 · Community 6337:4126 · Dailey Deals 6337:4462

  Panel geometry, identical in all six: content inset 20px from the viewport edges, so
  1400px of columns at a 1440 reference width.

  ONE DEFINITION, TWO PRESENTATIONS. `context` selects which:

    context: (omitted)   the desktop hover panel — a full-bleed row of columns plus the
                         ticker strip, hidden below 1280px
    context: 'mobile'    the same columns re-flowed as a stacked block for a level-2 panel
                         of the mobile drawer (snippets/aria-mobile-nav.liquid)

  The `case` below — which columns each parent has, their menus, widths, icons and copy —
  is NOT duplicated for mobile. Both presentations walk the identical branch and the same
  block settings, so adding a column or changing a menu handle updates desktop and mobile
  together. Only the wrapper markup differs here; the rest of the difference is CSS.

  The one CONTENT difference is product cards, which the mobile drawer must not render at
  all. That is carried by `col_context` on the `products` calls (see the note there) rather
  than hidden with CSS, so their images are never even referenced on mobile.

  Params: block (required), id (required), ticker (optional string),
          placeholders (optional bool — show the Figma row labels while a menu is empty),
          context (optional — 'mobile' for the drawer presentation)
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign panel_id = id
  assign is_mobile = false
  if context == 'mobile'
    assign is_mobile = true
  endif
  assign panel_slug = block.type | replace: '_mega_menu', '' | replace: '_', '-'

  comment
    The provided handles, preset per parent. Each is named after the column heading it
    feeds, so `aria-mega-column` takes the menu's own title as the heading and the literal
    strings below act only as fallbacks while a menu is still missing.
  endcomment
  assign h_shop_color = 'header-shop-shop-by-color'
  assign h_sh_basics = 'header-start-here-wig-101-the-basics'
  assign h_sh_guides = 'header-start-here-guides-answers'
  assign h_live_catchup = 'header-live-catch-up'
  assign h_live_schedule = 'header-live-this-week-s-schedule'
  assign h_comm_heart = 'header-community-our-heart'
  assign h_deals_save = 'header-dailey-deals-all-the-ways-to-save'

  comment
    Shop / Best Sellers / Live / Community run on a 24px column gap, Start Here / Deals
    on 20px.
  endcomment
  assign gap = 24
  if block.type == 'start_here_mega_menu' or block.type == 'daily_deals_mega_menu'
    assign gap = 20
  endif

  comment
    The row labels each Figma frame shows, kept here so a column whose Shopify menu does not
    exist yet still renders with the design's structure and copy length instead of a headed
    but empty box. They are used ONLY while that menu is missing — the moment it exists,
    Shopify's items replace them and these are ignored. The section's "Show placeholder rows"
    switch turns them off for launch.
  endcomment
  assign ph_shop_style = 'Long & Wavy|Mid-Length Lob|Short Bob|Pixie|Toppers'
  assign ph_shop_style_subs = 'soft, romantic volume|the everyday favorite|chic and easy|light and carefree|Add volume on top'
  assign ph_shop_color = 'City|Café Extended|Icons|Kristi Collection|Toppers'
  assign ph_sh_basics = 'How to measure your head|Wig cap construction explained|Washing & care|Color & fit guide'
  assign ph_sh_guides = 'Color Comparison|Wig catalogs|Wig collections|FAQ'
  assign ph_live_catchup = 'Watch past replays|This week’s new styles|How Live shopping works|Join the Facebook group'
  assign ph_live_schedule = 'Mon · New Arrivals|Wed · Dailey Deals|Fri · Community Try-On'
  assign ph_comm_heart = 'Kristi’s story|Our mission|Reviews & testimonials'
  assign ph_deals_save = 'Today’s Dailey Deals|Clearance / Retired|Last few in stock|Open box & SE|Shop all Sale'
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Both presentations keep the same two-element wrapper (outer + inner) so the tag structure
  is identical and only the class names and the desktop-only attributes change. Writing this
  as two separate `if` branches with their own opening and closing tags is how unbalanced
  Liquid markup happens.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div
  class="{% if is_mobile %}aria-mnav__mega aria-mnav__mega--{{ panel_slug }}{% else %}aria-mega aria-mega--{{ panel_slug }}{% endif %}"
  {% unless is_mobile %}
    id="{{ panel_id }}"
    data-aria-mega
    hidden
  {% endunless %}
  {% if block.type == 'live_mega_menu' %}data-lmu-root data-lmu-lazy{% endif %}
  style="--aria-mega-gap: {{ gap }}px;"
>
  <div class="{% if is_mobile %}aria-mnav__mega-inner{% else %}aria-mega__inner{% endif %}">
    {%- case block.type -%}

      {%- when 'shop_mega_menu' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Node 6337:4818 — 260/260/260, then a 60px void, then 244/244. The void is not
          hardcoded: column 4 carries `col_push` and the leftover width lands there.
          "Shop by Style" is the one column the design draws for which no handle was supplied, so it
          takes a menu PICKER rather than a pasted handle; its thumbnails and subtitles come
          from each linked collection's own image and description.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          ADDED 2026-10-26 — `.aria-mega__group--shop-grid` wraps Shop by Style (dead until
          style_menu is set), Shop by Collection and the 3 new filter columns below in a 4-up
          CSS grid (see assets/component-aria-mega-menu.css) that fills the space left of the
          two promo cards. None of the render calls inside it change; only this wrapper and
          the 3 new calls after "Shop by Color" are new. Figma node 7169:2908 ("Desktop /
          Shop").
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="aria-mega__group aria-mega__group--shop-grid">
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'style_cards', col_icon: 'mega-style', col_width: 260,
          col_heading: 'Shop by Style',
          col_menu_handle: block.settings.style_menu,
          col_placeholders: ph_shop_style, col_placeholder_subs: ph_shop_style_subs,
          placeholders: placeholders,
          shopify_attributes: block.shopify_attributes -%}
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'menu_divided', col_icon: 'mega-color', col_width: 260,
          col_heading: 'Shop by Color', col_menu_handle: h_shop_color,
          col_placeholders: ph_shop_color, placeholders: placeholders -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          UPDATED 2026-10-26 — By Cap Construction / Shop by Collection / Shop by Color / By
          Size & Length (Figma 7169:2960, 7169:2996, 7169:3033, 7169:3062) now read their
          items from a Shopify navigation menu picked per column (`cap_menu` /
          `collection_menu` / `color_menu` / `size_menu`, each a `shop_mega_menu` block
          setting) instead of per-item settings, so the client manages them from Content >
          Menus. Fixed left-to-right order per client decision: Cap Construction, Collection,
          Color, Size & Length. `collection_menu` defaults (header-group.json instance data,
          since a `link_list` setting has no schema "default") to the existing live handle so
          its output stays unchanged; the other three default to the 3 new menus made for
          this. A column hides itself when its menu is missing or empty — see `skip_col` in
          aria-mega-column.liquid.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'items_photos',
          col_heading: block.settings.cap_heading,
          col_icon_image: block.settings.cap_icon, col_icon_fallback: 'wp-mega-construction-icon.svg',
          col_menu_handle: block.settings.cap_menu,
          col_item_prefix: 'cap_item_',
          col_default_images: 'wp-mega-construction-hand-tied.png|wp-mega-construction-extended-lace.png|wp-mega-construction-full-mono.png|wp-mega-construction-mono-topper.png',
          block: block -%}
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'items_divided',
          col_heading: block.settings.collection_heading,
          col_icon_image: block.settings.collection_icon, col_icon: 'mega-collection',
          col_menu_handle: block.settings.collection_menu -%}
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'items_divided',
          col_heading: block.settings.color_heading,
          col_icon_image: block.settings.color_icon, col_icon_fallback: 'wp-mega-color-icon.svg',
          col_menu_handle: block.settings.color_menu -%}
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'items_divided',
          col_heading: block.settings.size_heading,
          col_icon_image: block.settings.size_icon, col_icon_fallback: 'wp-mega-size-icon.svg',
          col_menu_handle: block.settings.size_menu -%}
        </div>
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'promo_card', col_icon: 'mega-bestseller', col_icon_tone: 'qi',
          col_width: 244,
          col_push: true, col_heading: 'Best Seller Style',
          col_image: block.settings.promo_1_image,
          col_chip: block.settings.promo_1_badge,
          col_chip_style: block.settings.promo_1_badge_style,
          col_btn_label: block.settings.promo_1_button_label,
          col_btn_url: block.settings.promo_1_button_url -%}
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'promo_card', col_icon: 'mega-daily', col_width: 244,
          col_heading: 'New markdown daily',
          col_image: block.settings.promo_2_image,
          col_chip: block.settings.promo_2_badge,
          col_chip_style: block.settings.promo_2_badge_style,
          col_btn_label: block.settings.promo_2_button_label,
          col_btn_url: block.settings.promo_2_button_url -%}

      {%- when 'best_sellers_mega_menu' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Node 6337:3198 — a 300x449 feature card, then a 1076px products column pushed to
          the right edge. 1076 is the OUTER width: the column carries the design's 20px
          side padding, leaving 1036 of cards, which divides into exactly 4 x 250 on 12px
          gaps. Feeding 1036 as the width (an earlier pass) shrank every card by 10px.

          NO `col_shell` here. Unlike Start Here and Deals, this row sits on bare white
          (verified against 6337:3210 — pure #FFFFFF behind the cards); the gradient that
          used to be on every products column was the unwanted background.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'feature_card', col_width: 300,
          col_variant: 'best-sellers',
          col_image: block.settings.feature_image,
          col_chip: block.settings.feature_heading,
          col_body: block.settings.feature_text,
          col_btn_label: block.settings.feature_button_label,
          col_btn_url: block.settings.feature_button_url,
          shopify_attributes: block.shopify_attributes -%}
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'products', col_context: context, col_icon: 'mega-bestseller', col_icon_tone: 'qi',
          col_width: 1076,
          col_push: true,
          col_heading: block.settings.products_heading,
          col_collection: block.settings.collection,
          col_count: 4, panel_id: panel_id -%}

      {%- when 'start_here_mega_menu' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Node 6337:3498 — two outlined-card menu columns (284 / 260) on a 20px gap, then
          the products column pushed right at an OUTER 814 (20px of shell padding either
          side, 774 of cards = 3 x 250 on 12px gaps). This one DOES take the gradient
          shell (6337:3548).

          284 is not decorative: the design's longest row, "Wig cap construction
          explained", measures 254px and the row insets it 12px each side, so anything
          under ~278 wraps it to two lines.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'menu_padded', col_icon: 'mega-collection', col_width: 284,
          col_heading: 'Wig 101: The Basics', col_menu_handle: h_sh_basics,
          col_placeholders: ph_sh_basics, placeholders: placeholders,
          shopify_attributes: block.shopify_attributes -%}
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'menu_padded', col_icon: 'mega-color', col_width: 260,
          col_heading: 'Guides & Answers', col_menu_handle: h_sh_guides,
          col_placeholders: ph_sh_guides, placeholders: placeholders -%}
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'products', col_context: context, col_icon: 'mega-bestseller', col_icon_tone: 'qi',
          col_width: 814, col_shell: true,
          col_push: true,
          col_heading: block.settings.products_heading,
          col_collection: block.settings.collection,
          col_count: 3, panel_id: panel_id -%}

      {%- when 'live_mega_menu' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Node 6337:3897 — 375 / 376 outlined-card menu columns, then a 493px media card
          pushed right. Its heading is the one column label the design sets in
          Primary/Dark Pink rather than black, hence `col_title_tone: 'accent'`.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'menu_padded', col_icon: 'mega-collection', col_width: 375,
          col_heading: 'Catch Up', col_menu_handle: h_live_catchup,
          col_placeholders: ph_live_catchup, placeholders: placeholders,
          shopify_attributes: block.shopify_attributes -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The schedule and the media card come from the LiveMeUp app (the shows actually
          booked, and the one on air / next / latest), loaded the first time the menu opens.
          The header-live-this-week-s-schedule menu is no longer read.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- render 'aria-livemeup' -%}
        {%- assign lmu_live_url = block.settings.media_button_url | default: '/pages/live' -%}
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'lmu_schedule', col_icon: 'mega-calendar', col_width: 376,
          col_heading: 'This Week’s Schedule', col_count: 4,
          col_btn_url: lmu_live_url -%}
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'media_card', col_icon: 'mega-live', col_width: 493,
          col_title_tone: 'accent',
          col_lmu: true,
          col_push: true,
          col_heading: block.settings.media_heading,
          col_image: block.settings.media_image,
          col_btn_label: block.settings.media_button_label,
          col_btn_url: block.settings.media_button_url -%}

      {%- when 'community_mega_menu' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Node 6337:4238 — a 378 feature column (20px of gradient-shell padding either
          side of a 338 card), a 515 photo row, and a 320 menu column. This is the one
          panel whose last column is NOT flush right (the design leaves 139px of trailing
          space), so no column here carries `col_push`. Its feature card has a heading and
          no icon, and — unlike Best Sellers and Deals — NO PHOTO.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'feature_card', col_width: 378, col_shell: true,
          col_variant: 'community',
          col_heading: 'The Sisterhood',
          col_image: block.settings.feature_image,
          col_chip: block.settings.feature_heading,
          col_body: block.settings.feature_text,
          col_btn_label: block.settings.feature_button_label,
          col_btn_url: block.settings.feature_button_url,
          shopify_attributes: block.shopify_attributes -%}
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'photo_row', col_icon: 'mega-calendar', col_width: 515,
          col_heading: 'Real Women, Real Wigs',
          col_collection: block.settings.gallery_collection,
          col_btn_label: block.settings.gallery_button_label,
          col_btn_url: block.settings.gallery_button_url -%}
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'menu_padded', col_icon: 'mega-collection', col_width: 320,
          col_heading: 'Our Heart', col_menu_handle: h_comm_heart,
          col_placeholders: ph_comm_heart, placeholders: placeholders -%}

      {%- when 'daily_deals_mega_menu' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Node 6337:4512 — a 260x450 feature card, a 284 menu column on a 20px gap, then
          the products column pushed right at an OUTER 814 with the gradient shell
          (6337:4546). The design badges these cards with copy ("Dailey Deal") rather than
          the best-seller rank, so the badge is a setting here.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'feature_card', col_width: 260,
          col_variant: 'deals',
          col_image: block.settings.feature_image,
          col_chip: block.settings.feature_heading,
          col_body: block.settings.feature_text,
          col_btn_label: block.settings.feature_button_label,
          col_btn_url: block.settings.feature_button_url,
          shopify_attributes: block.shopify_attributes -%}
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'menu_padded', col_icon: 'mega-collection', col_width: 284,
          col_heading: 'All the Ways to Save', col_menu_handle: h_deals_save,
          col_placeholders: ph_deals_save, placeholders: placeholders -%}
        {%- render 'aria-mega-column',
          col_type: 'products', col_context: context, col_icon: 'mega-bestseller', col_icon_tone: 'qi',
          col_width: 814, col_shell: true,
          col_push: true,
          col_heading: block.settings.products_heading,
          col_collection: block.settings.collection,
          col_count: 3,
          col_chip: block.settings.product_badge,
          col_chip_style: block.settings.product_badge_style, panel_id: panel_id -%}

    {%- endcase -%}
  </div>

  {%- if ticker != blank and is_mobile == false -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Every desktop panel closes with the same full-width 44px promo strip (node
      6337:3294), so the copy is one section setting rather than six block settings.

      The drawer omits it: the strip is a full-bleed band spanning the viewport under the
      panel, which has no equivalent inside a 360px-wide drawer, and repeating it at the
      foot of all six level-2 panels would be noise rather than the design.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="aria-mega__ticker">
      <span class="aria-mega__ticker-text">{{ ticker }}</span>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
